  1194:<h3 id="hibernate-gsg-tutorial-jpa-config">4.1. persistence.xml</h3>
  1196:<p>The previous tutorials used the Hibernate-specific <code>hibernate.cfg.xml</code> configuration file.  Jakarta Persistence, however, defines
  1197:a different bootstrap process that uses its own configuration file named <code>persistence.xml</code>.  This bootstrapping process
  1198:is defined by the Jakarta Persistence specification.  In Java&#8482; SE environments the persistence provider (Hibernate in this case)
  1199:is required to locate all Jakarta Persistence configuration files by classpath lookup of the <code>META-INF/persistence.xml</code> resource name.</p>
  1202:<div class="title">Example 10. persistence.xml</div>
  1219:<p><code>persistence.xml</code> files should provide a unique name for each "persistence unit".  Applications use this name to
  1249:<p>The previous tutorials used the Hibernate native APIs.  This tutorial uses the Jakarta Persistence APIs.</p>
  1264:<p>Notice again that the persistence unit name is <code>org.hibernate.tutorial.jpa</code>, which matches <a href="#hibernate-gsg-tutorial-jpa-config-pu">persistence.xml</a>.</p>
  1283:is used instead of the <code>org.hibernate.Session</code> interface.  Jakarta Persistence calls this operation "persist" instead of "save".</p>
