r,#content h1>a.anchor:hover,h2:hover>a.anchor,h2>a.anchor:hover,h3:hover>a.anchor,#toctitle:hover>a.anchor,.sidebarblock>.content>.title:hover>a.anchor,h3>a.anchor:hover,#toctitle>a.anchor:hover,.sidebarblock>.content>.title>a.anchor:hover,h4:hover>a.anchor,h4>a.anchor:hover,h5:hover>a.anchor,h5>a.anchor:hover,h6:hover>a.anchor,h6>a.anchor:hover{visibility:visible}\n196:#content h1>a.link,h2>a.link,h3>a.link,#toctitle>a.link,.sidebarblock>.content>.title>a.link,h4>a.link,h5>a.link,h6>a.link{color:#ba3925;text-decoration:none}\n197:#content h1>a.link:hover,h2>a.link:hover,h3>a.link:hover,#toctitle>a.link:hover,.sidebarblock>.content>.title>a.link:hover,h4>a.link:hover,h5>a.link:hover,h6>a.link:hover{color:#a53221}\n396:h1,h2,p,td.content,span.alt{letter-spacing:-.01em}\n414:h2,h3,#toctitle,.sidebarblock>.content>.title{page-break-after:avoid}\n424:body.book #toc,body.book #preamble,body.book h1.sect0,body.book .sect1>h2{page-break-before:always}\n474:<li><a href=\"#tutorial_jpa\">4. Tutorial Using the Java Persistence API (Jakarta Persistence)</a>\n476:<li><a href=\"#hibernate-gsg-tutorial-jpa-config\">4.1. persistence.xml</a></li>\n484:<li><a href=\"#hibernate-gsg-tutorial-envers-config\">5.1. persistence.xml</a></li>\n495:<h2 id=\"preface\">Preface</h2>\n549:<h2 id=\"obtaining\">1. Obtaining Hibernate</h2>\n682:<h2 id=\"tutorial-native\">2. Tutorial Using Native Hibernate APIs and hbm.xml Mapping</h2>\n717:define JDBC connection information. These tutorials utilize the H2 in-memory database, so the values of these properties\n718:are all specific to running H2 in its in-memory mode.  <code>connection.pool_size</code> is used to configure the number of\n1027:<h2 id=\"tutorial_annotations\">3. Tutorial Using Native Hibernate APIs and Annotation Mappings</h2>\n1165:<h2 id=\"tutorial_jpa\">4. Tutorial Using the Java Persistence API (Jakarta Persistence)</h2>\n1183:<p><i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\"></i> Bootstrap a Jakarta Persistence <code>EntityManagerFactory</code></p>\n1189:<p><i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\"></i> Use Jakarta Persistence API calls</p>\n1194:<h3 id=\"hibernate-gsg-tutorial-jpa-config\">4.1. persistence.xml</h3>\n1196:<p>The previous tutorials used the Hibernate-specific <code>hibernate.cfg.xml</code> configuration file.  Jakarta Persistence, however, defines\n1197:a different bootstrap process that uses its own configuration file named <code>persistence.xml</code>.  This bootstrapping process\n1198:is defined by the Jakarta Persistence specification.  In Java&#8482; SE environments the persistence provider (Hibernate in this case)\n1199:is required to locate all Jakarta Persistence configuration files by classpath lookup of the <code>META-INF/persistence.xml</code> resource name.</p>\n1202:<div class=\"title\">Example 10. persistence.xml</div>\n1219:<p><code>persistence.xml</code> files should provide a unique name for each \"persistence unit\".  Applications use this name to\n1249:<p>The previous tutorials used the Hibernate native APIs.  This tutorial uses the Jakarta Persistence APIs.</p>\n1264:<p>Notice again that the persistence unit name is <code>org.hibernate.tutorial.jpa</code>, which matches <a href=\"#hibernate-gsg-tutorial-jpa-config-pu\">persistence.xml</a>.</p>\n1283:is used instead of the <code>org.hibernate.Session</code> interface.  Jakarta Persistence calls this operation \"persist\" instead of \"save\".</p>\n1324:<h2 id=\"tutorial_envers\">5. Tutorial Using Envers</h2>\n1353:<h3 id=\"hibernate-gsg-tutorial-envers-config\">5.1. persistence.xml</h3>\n1355:<p>This file was discussed in the Jakarta Persistence tutorial in <a href=\"#hibernate-gsg-tutorial-jpa-config\">persistence.xml</a>, and is essentially the same here.</p>\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1785245566237}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_I2Lu8xNrnwq3HrFveNuHrSXU|fc_0c66e1fe53f76537016a68af7cfe64819a8f3bb052c3d988a7", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "/*\n * Copyright and related rights waived via CC0\n *\n * You should have received a copy of the CC0 legalcode along with this\n * work. If not, see <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/>.\n */\npackage org_hibernate.hibernate_core;\n\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\n\nimport java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\n\nimport static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;\n\npublic class IdentifierGeneratorTest {\n\n    private static final Class[] identifierGenerators = new Class[]{\n            org.hibernate.id.UUIDGenerator.class,\n            org.hibernate.id.GUIDGenerator.class,\n            org.hibernate.id.UUIDHexGenerator.class,\n            org.hibernate.id.Assigned.class,\n            org.hibernate.id.IdentityGenerator.class,\n            org.hibernate.id.SelectGenerator.class,\n            org.hibernate.id.enhanced.SequenceStyleGenerator.class,\n            org.hibernate.id.IncrementGenerator.class,\n            org.hibernate.id.ForeignGenerator.class\n    };\n\n    @Test\n    public void testIdentifierGenerators() throws Exception {\n        for (Class clazz : identifierGenerators) {\n            Constructor constructor = clazz.getConstructor();\n            assertThat(constructor).isNotNull();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1785245566237}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_Slhq7y3SUT1Xf44NBKQ7gXvg|fc_0c66e1fe53f76537016a68af7cfe70819abf15a5be95750077", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<configuration>\n\n    <appender name=\"STDOUT\" class=\"ch.qos.logback.core.ConsoleAppender\">\n        <encoder>\n            <pattern>%d{HH:mm:ss.SSS} [%thread] %-5level %logger{36} - %msg%n</pattern>\n        </encoder>\n    </appender>\n\n    <logger name=\"org.hibernate.SQL\" level=\"DEBUG\"/>\n\n    <logger name=\"org.hibernate.hql.internal.ast.QueryTranslatorImpl\" level=\"DEBUG\"/>\n\n    <root level=\"ERROR\">\n        <appender-ref ref=\"STDOUT\" />\n    </root>\n\n</configuration>\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1785245566238}]}
